§ `Chapter 6 — Change, reinstatement and termination`

-- src:1885 | CHƯƠNG 6: THAY ĐỔI - KHÔI PHỤC - CHẤM DỨT HỢP ĐỒNG BẢO HIỂM

§§ `Article 21 — Refusing the insurance (the free look)`

-- src:1887 | Điều 21: Từ chối tham gia bảo hiểm
-- src:1888 | Bên mua bảo hiểm có quyền từ chối tham gia bảo hiểm trong vòng 21 (hai mươi mốt) ngày
-- src:1889 | kể từ ngày phát hành Hợp đồng bảo hiểm và Bên mua bảo hiểm đã nhận được bộ Hợp đồng
-- src:1890 | bảo hiểm. Công ty sẽ hoàn lại số phí bảo hiểm mà Bên mua bảo hiểm đã đóng, không có lãi,
-- src:1891 | sau khi trừ đi các chi phí kiểm tra sức khỏe, nếu có.
-- "trong vòng 21 (hai mươi mốt) ngày kể từ ngày phát hành Hợp đồng bảo hiểm và Bên mua bảo
-- hiểm đã nhận được bộ Hợp đồng bảo hiểm": read as counting from the day on which BOTH have
-- happened, the later of issue and receipt (fork F20). Read as counting from issue, with
-- receipt a mere condition, the period shrinks by however long delivery took (finding FD13).
-- LAW: Article 35 of the Law on Insurance Business (aid, line 760) counts 21 days from
-- receipt. Day 21 after the start is the last day.
@ref V082021 Article 21 (src:1888-1889)
GIVEN f IS A `A free-look refusal`
GIVETH A DATE
`21 — the day the free-look period counts from, for` f MEANS
    IF   f's `date the policyholder received the contract` GREATER THAN f's `date the contract was issued`
    THEN f's `date the policyholder received the contract`
    ELSE f's `date the contract was issued`

@ref V082021 Article 21 (src:1888-1889)
GIVEN f IS A `A free-look refusal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`21 — the refusal is in time` f MEANS
        f's `date of the refusal` AT LEAST f's `date the policyholder received the contract`
    AND f's `date of the refusal` AT MOST  (`21 — the day the free-look period counts from, for` f PLUS 21)

-- Finding FD13: the clock read from issue.
@ref V082021 Article 21 (src:1888-1889), counted from issue
GIVEN f IS A `A free-look refusal`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`21, counted from issue — the refusal is in time` f MEANS
        f's `date of the refusal` AT LEAST f's `date the policyholder received the contract`
    AND f's `date of the refusal` AT MOST  (f's `date the contract was issued` PLUS 21)

@ref V082021 Article 21 (src:1890-1891)
GIVEN f IS A `A free-look refusal`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`21 — the premiums refunded` f MEANS
    f's `premiums paid` MINUS f's `medical examination costs`

-- The right as a regulative rule, on a clock of days from the start of the period. The
-- refund has no deadline in Article 21; the duty is written without one.
@ref V082021 Article 21 (src:1888-1891)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `A party` `An act under the contract`
`21 — the free-look right` MEANS
    PARTY `the policyholder`
    MAY   `refuse to continue the insurance`
    WITHIN 21
    HENCE PARTY `the Company`
          MUST  `refund the premiums paid, without interest, less medical examination costs`

§§ `Article 22 — Changes concerning the contract`

